Package: platypus
Type: Package
Title: Computer Vision for Medical Imaging
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: person("Michal", "Maj", email = "michalmaj116@gmail.com",
                  role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Semantic segmentation and object detection for medical images, from a
    folder of pictures to a trained model and a figure, in a handful of lines or one
    configuration file. Architectures, losses and training run on PyTorch through the
    'pyplatypus' Python package, which is installed and isolated automatically; nothing
    has to be set up by hand. R keeps the parts that make an analysis fast - reading and
    combining masks, drawing boxes, plotting, comparing models.
